Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: mask HFI and clear stale status before GMU boot

HFI boot replies and OOB acknowledgements are polled. Mask the IRQ line
and clear stale status while the firmware is still stopped. Only unmask
CM3 faults after HFI starts; a fresh fault remains latched for the ISR.

OEM: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource, liuqin-t-oss
     eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e, drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_gen7_gmu.c.
     gen7_gmu_irq_enable() clears pending status and programs the IRQ
     masks before gen7_gmu_device_start(). The mask used here reflects
     the Linux driver's polled HFI replies and OOB acknowledgements.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 3f0340d8e..42ec70ecd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1363,6 +1363,10 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	/* Set the bus quota to a reasonable value for boot */
 	a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(gpu, gmu);
 
+	/* HFI boot replies are polled. Keep them off the IRQ line at startup. */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK, ~0);
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, ~0);
+
 	/* Enable the GMU interrupt */
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_CLR, ~0);
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_MASK, ~A6XX_GMU_IRQ_MASK);
@@ -1407,7 +1411,6 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	 * Turn on the GMU firmware fault interrupt after we know the boot
 	 * sequence is successful
 	 */
-	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, ~0);
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK, ~A6XX_HFI_IRQ_MASK);
 	enable_irq(gmu->hfi_irq);
 
